 should be readable and clearly connected to the right part","Careful use of diagram and explain why it matters with clear evidence","Tiny squeezed labels can make an accurate diagram unusable","Handwriting on labelled diagrams must stay legible, with labels placed clearly and leader lines that point to the"],"question":"Which statement is a common mistake when working with label?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Understanding is shown by new evidence and a named diagram and explain why it matters, not by copying the model. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Apply label to new material and name the diagram and explain why it matters used","Repeat the worked example wording with no new evidence","Tiny squeezed labels can make an accurate diagram unusable","Name diagram and explain why it matters only, without linking it to label"],"question":"Which response best applies label with new evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"The skill is shown by quoting or pointing to wording that carries label. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Tiny squeezed labels can make an accurate diagram unusable","Point to exact words in the sentence that show label and say what they do","Ignore the sentence and invent a more exciting event","Say the writing is good without naming any words"],"question":"Read: \"When the ferry horn blasted, Omar gripped the railing and laughed.\" Which choice best uses label from this lesson?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"The correct statement applies the language skill with textual evidence. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Tiny squeezed labels can make an accurate diagram unusable","Copy a model sentence from another story unchanged","Name diagram and explain why it matters without linking it to any words in the text","Each label should be readable and clea